{"id":"000W2K","title":"Let's Go Round Again! (toroidal x-sums)","author":"Chilly","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-18T14:10:29+00:00","posted":"Heute, 10:50 Uhr","rules":"I just published some newer chaos construction puzzles as part of Myxo's Chaotic Construction series, so it's time for something different.\n\nThis is one I first set a few years ago, but then re-worked for a pack Bremster was putting together. Now it can finally get published here. Please enjoy.\n\nThe Rules:\n\n• Normal Sudoku rules apply.\n• Numbers outside the grid are two-cell X-sums clues. The sum of the digits in the first two cells in the row or column next to a clue gives the number, N, of cells that contribute to the X-sum total in that row or column. The X-sum total is given by adding the first N digits in the row or column, moving away from the clue. Rows and columns are toroidal, so if N>9 then the next cell after cell 9 will be cell 1 again, and so on.\n\nLet's Go Round Again!\nby Chilly\n\nLink for solving on Sudokupad","solutionCode":"Column 4","tags":["Sudoku","X-Sums (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/z13hbl740n","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/z13hbl740n","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-18T14:10:29+00:00"}